      "message": "If a driver exposes a 4KB-aligned (non-16KB-aligned) physical range via `vm_iomap_memory(vma, start, len)` with `vma-\u003evm_pgoff \u003d\u003d 0` and `vma-\u003evm_slice_off \u003d\u003d 0`, `pfn \u003d start \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT_KERNEL` discards bits `[13:12]` of `start` and maps slice 0 of the enclosing 16KB frame instead of the subpage slice at `start \u0026 ~PAGE_MASK_KERNEL`. In addition, if a driver resets `vma-\u003evm_pgoff \u003d 0` without clearing `vma-\u003evm_slice_off` (e.g. after using `vm_pgoff` as an `mmap` cookie), `vma_kernel_pages(vma)` and `vma_remap_frame()` will use the stale `vm_slice_off`.\n\n**Recommendation**: Please squash aosp/4368009 (`p3s_6.18_b16`: `ANDROID: P3S: mm: Map 4KB-aligned physical ranges in vm_iomap_memory()`) into this change.",
